2 CONT    1 --    Sawatzky, Daniel (#197182) 26 December 1778, Pordenau, Gross Werder, Prussia
2 CONT    2 --    Sawatzky, Maria (#197183) 11 February 1781, Pordenau, Gross Werder, Prussia
2 CONT    3 -- + Sawatzky, Anna (#197184) About 1784, Prussia
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Note: In the 1776 census of Mennonites in West Prussia he is listed in Pordenau with 1 son and 3 daughters. He was a member of the Ladekopp Flemish Gemeinde. He migrated from Prussia to Kronsweide, Chortitza, S. Russia in 1789 (P.
2 CONC  Rempel, p. 25). He probably died by 1793 since he is not listed in the 1793 Chortitza Colony Heads of Households List and had certainly died by 1795 since his widow Maria had remarried to Peter Schmidt by 1795 (B. H. Unruh, p. 24
2 CONC 2, 253). Many of his children came to the Molotschna Colony. He may have been related to Thomas Sawatzky #197174 and/or Johann Sowatzki (b. 8 Apr 1712) #8407, but there is no definitive evidence of this.
