1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2025 04 27: As suggested by Wendy Sue Barg: 
2 CONT Anna ? is his 1st wife with children Johann (Abt. 1753), Thomas (Abt. 1754), and Peter Thomas (4 July 1760). I have also assigned dates for Anna -- Born about 1725 and Died before 1781.
2 CONT Elisabeth Enz is his 2nd wife (born abt. 1757) married About 1781 with children Cornelius Thomas (23 Sept 1781) and Sara (Abt. 1783). 
2 CONT This has not been changed until we get clarification on this, however, logic says this has to be correct.
2 CONT =======
2 CONT Thomas J. Sawatzky #100953 
2 CONT Born: Prussia
2 CONT Residence: 1784, Rosenort, Gross Werder, Prussia
2 CONT Last update of Individual data: 26 October 2024
2 CONT Family  1:  #509938	
2 CONT Spouse: Enz, Elisabeth (#1402719) abt 1757
2 CONT Family  2:  #2536	
2 CONT Spouse: _?_, Anna (#197175)
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT    1 --    Sawatzky, Johann (#1562080) abt 1753
2 CONT    2 --    Sawatzky, Thomas (#1562079) abt 1754
2 CONT    3 -- + Sawatzky, Peter T. (#156770) 4 July 1760, Prussia
2 CONT    4 -- + Sawatzky, Cornelius Thomas (#3857) 23 September 1781, Heubuden, Gross Werder, Prussia
2 CONT    5 --    Sawatzky, Sara (#46489) About 1783, Prussia
2 CONT GRanDMA Notes:	
2 CONT Note: In the 1776 census of Mennonites in West Prussia he is listed in Walldorf with 2 sons. He may have been related to Daniel Sawatzky #197177 and/or Johann Sowatzki (b. 8 Apr 1712) #8407, but there is no definitive evidence of 
2 CONC this. The 1835 Molotschna Census entry for his son Cornelius clearly indicates that his name was Thomas. 
2 CONT ='''It has been suggested that he was the son of Hans Sawatsky, #8405.'''=  
2 CONT See Henry Schapansky 'The Bergthaler Sawatskys', Preservings No.9, Dec. 1996.
2 CONT Note: All of his children are listed under one mother but were not all her children. 
2 CONT ====
2 CONT Potential Middle Name: Johann
2 CONT Potential Birth & Death Dates & Places:
2 CONT Birth:	1733
2 CONT Werder, Demmin, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, Germany
2 CONT Death:	1780 (46-47)
2 CONT Danzig, West Prussia
2 CONT ==========
2 CONT Requires more research.... ?.?.? Potential match Thomas Sawatzky 
2 CONT #100953    /208th  
2 CONT Birth:	Prussia 
2 CONT Last update:	30 Jun 2019 Family: Family 60374 	
2 CONT Spouse:  _?_, Anna,  1735, #197175 
2 CONT Last update:      2/13/2018 
2 CONT 1 -- +  Sawatzky, Cornelius Thomas,  23 Sep 1781, #3857 
2 CONT 2 --     Sawatzky, Sara,  Abt 1784, #46489 
2 CONT Notes:	 Note: In the 1776 W. Prussia Census he is listed in Walldorf with 2 sons (H. Penner, p. 456). He may have been related to Daniel Sawatzky #197177 and/or Johann Sowatzki (b. 8 Apr 1712) #8407, but there is no definitive evi
2 CONC dence of this. The 1835 Molotschna Census entry for his son Cornelius clearly indicates that his name was Thomas. Thomas lived in Walldorf at the time of the 1776 Prussian census, along with two sons. They were part of the Rosenor
2 CONC t congregation. It has been suggested that he was the son of Hans Sawatsky, #8405. See Henry Schapansky 'The Bergthaler Sawatskys', Preservings No.9, Dec. 1996. Birth Source: Chortitza: The Old Colony Russia - The First Settlers; 
2 CONC Schapansky, Henry; Mennonite Family History Birth Source: Harder, Stanley, e-mail 30 May 1998 Source: Harder, Stanley; Gedcom File, Aug 2001 Source: Broesky, John. BK6 update to GM423
2 CONT
2 CONT ???? Potential father  Hans Sawatzky 
