2 CONT    1 --   Sawatzky, Daniel About 1790, Prussia1,3,8,9
2 CONT    2 -- +Sawatzky, Maria 1 September 1797, Spittelhoff, Elbing, Prussia1,3,8,11,12,13,14
2 CONT    3 -- +Sawatsky, Jacob Johann About 1800, Prussia1,3,8,9,15,16,17
2 CONT    4 --   Sawatzky, Johann About 1802, Prussia2,3
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Emigration note: Applied to emigrate.
2 CONT Note: According to his emigration application he had been a "Viehpaechter" from Spittelhoff for the past 10 years. Included in the application was 14 year-old Gertruda Rempel [#46499 - see her notes]. He migrated from Spittelhoff,
2 CONC  Amt Elbing, Prussia, to Russia in 1804 (B. H. Unruh, p. 319, 352; P. Rempel, p. 79). He appears to have settled in Ladekop, Molotschna Colony since his family is listed at Ladekop #20 in the 1806 and 1808 Censuses (B. H. Unruh, p
2 CONC . 319). He had died by 1806 since his widow had remarried to Jacob Loewen by the time the 1806 Census was compiled. Also migrating with him in 1804 was a "maid" Gertruda Rempel (b. ca 1788) #46499 (B. H. Unruh, p. 352).
