2 CONC y, Peter,  #3861, 5 SEP 1828,  Ohrloff, Molotschna, South Russia Notes:	 Note: In the 1808 Molotschna Colony Census he is listed at Ohrloff #3 and is said to have come from Heubuden, Prussia (B. H. Unruh, p. 324). However, the mig
2 CONC ration list (Unruh, p. 352) says that he came in 1804 from Ellerwald, 4th. Trift, Prussia. Also listed as migrating with him was a Sara Sawatzki, born abt 1784. Could this be a sister? JMH says that he was married in 1805. He was 
2 CONC listed at Ohrloff #3 in 1815 at the time of the birth of his daughter Sara per the 1815-1816 Molotschna Colony Vital Records. In the 1835 Census he is listed at Ohrloff #3, where it says he came to Russia in 1804. Source: Friesen,
2 CONC  Heinrich Familien Register; Friesen, Heinrich, page p. 7 Marriage Source: Profile of the Mennonite Kleine Gemeinde 1874; Plett, Delbert F. ed.; DFP Publications, Box 1960 Steinbach, Manitoba, 1987, 312 pp., page 274
