1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The couple's two eldest children, Jacob, Jr. and Ann (wo married John Aldaffer), were born in Virginia. After 1790 and before 1800, Jacob and Elizabeth move to an unknown county in South Carolina. By 1820 they were
2 CONC  residing in Richland County, S.C. (near Columbia). Eight Children were born to them while they lived in South Carolina:  Josiah Born 1800 S.C. Died ? ? John M. Born 1800/1810 S.C. Died ? ? Daughter Born 1794/1804 S.C. Died ? ? Da
2 CONC ughter2 Born 1804/1810 S.C. Died ? ? William Born 1810 S.C. Died 1889 Ga. Newman3 Born 1814 S.C. Died 1901 Ala. Martha Born 1817 S.C. Died 1907 Ga. Daughter Born 1810/1820 S.C. Died ? ?  By 1827 Elizabeth was a widow living in Was
2 CONC hington County, Georgia, with part of her children. As a three year resident of the state, she was eligible to draw in the Land Lottery of Georgia of 1827. Elizabeth was designated as a "fortunate drawer" as she was awarded land i
2 CONC n this lottery. This was a parcel of 202.5 acres in western Georgia. It can be assumed that Elizabeth Shirey died after 1840 in Gwinnett County, Georgia, where she had been living with her son John M. Shirey and his family. 
2 CONT
