2 CONT ------------
2 CONT Heinrich Heinrich Wiens
2 CONT #46998 
2 CONT Birth:	Born: 7 July 1774, Elbing, Elbing, Prussia
2 CONT Death:	Died: 1820, Blumenort, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT Facts & events:	Emigrated: 13 August 1803
2 CONT Immigrated: arrived 1804
2 CONT  Last update of Individual data: 30 October 2024
2 CONT Parents: Family #32457	
2 CONT Father: Wiens, Heinrich (#518931)
2 CONT Family :  #32456	
2 CONT Spouse: Sawatzky, Judith (#46999) About 1774, Elbing, Elbing, Prussia
2 CONT Married: About 1798
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT    1 --    Wiens, Judith (#70162) June 1800, Elbing, Elbing, Prussia
2 CONT    2 --    Wiens, Gertruda (#70161) 5 September 1803, Schottland, Danzig, Prussia
2 CONT    3 -- + Wiens, Margaretha (#52656) 21 January 1807, Blumenort, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT    4 --    Wiens, Helena (#936074) 1809, Blumenort, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT    5 --    Wiens, Catarina (#936073) About 1812
2 CONT    6 -- + Wiens, Heinrich (#60807) 11 November 1813, Blumenort, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT    7 -- + Wiens, Gerhard Heinrich (#60810) 12 July 1816, Blumenort, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Emigration note: Applied to emigrate.
2 CONT Note: According to his emigration application he was a "Hauszimmergeselle" [apprentice carpenter] from "Vorberge", which was part of the city of Elbing. In the 1808 Molotschna Colony Census he is listed at Blumenort #10 and is sai
2 CONC d to have come from Elbing, Prussia (B. H. Unruh, p. 327). He was listed at Blumenort #10 in 1816 at the time of the birth of his son Gerhard per the 1815-1816 Molotschna Colony Vital Records. The 1835 Molotschna Census entry for 
2 CONC Blumenort #10 says that he died in 1820. His sons are listed at that address as stepsons of Peter Willems #60811, but the Willems' wife is too young to be their mother. Suffice it to say, there is some "step" relationship between 
2 CONC Willems and the Wiens boys, but further clarification is needed to pinpoint it exactly! See note for Judith Sawatzky. He came to Russia in 1804. He was a carpenter. His age is incorrectly given as 35 in the 1806 Molotschna Colony 
2 CONC Census.
2 CONT Copied from GRanDMA July 5, 2025
