2 CONT Name	Anna F. SAWATZKY  Born	17 Sep 1809 	Ohrloff, Molotschna Colony, South Russia Find all individuals with events at this location  Gender	Female  History	Anna F. Sawatzky married Isaac Harms, the son of Johan Harms, who settled 
2 CONC in the village of Blumenstein, Molotschna in 1804. Isaac Harms is recognized as being one of the most significant supporters of the Kleine Gemeinde resettlement program for its landless during the 1860's. In 1864, the family moved
2 CONC  to Markuslandt which Isaac Harms had been instrumental in founding. In 1874, the Harms family moved to Jansen, Nebraska where Isaac Harms married for a second time to Karolina Plett, the widow of his wife's uncle, Klaas Friesen. 
2 CONC Son Cornelius remained in Russia, resident in Schönau, Molotschna in 1892, but by 1913, he was a resident in California.  [2]  Immigration	17 Jul 1874 	Hammonia; New York Find all individuals with events at this location  [3]  Ref
2 CONC erence Number	208an  Religion	Mennonite  Died	6 Apr 1877 	Jansen, Jefferson, Nebraska Find all individuals with events at this location  Person ID	I471 	Reid Family | Lynn's side of the family Last Modified	12 Jul 2013 
