1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500's-1900's
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Christoffel Doll 
2 CONT
2 CONT Year: 1739  
2 CONT
2 CONT Place: Pennsylvania  
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members: Father Christoffel; Child Johann Nickel; Child Johann Abraham; Child; Child Maria Engel; Sister Anna Maria Margretha; Sister Anna Catharina; Brother-in-law; Mother Sara Schuch  
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Publication Code: 1031.9  
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary Immigrant: Doll, Casper 
2 CONT
2 CONT Annotation: Date and port of arrival or date and place of naturalization. Span indicates period between last mention of emigrant in country of origin and first mention of his residence in the New World. "Surname, ..." indicates a 
2 CONC variation of a surname.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Bibliography: BURGERT, ANNETTE KUNSELMAN. Eighteenth Century Emigrants from German-Speaking Lands to North America. Publications of the Pennsylvania German Society, 16/19. Birdsboro, PA: The Pennsylvania German Society. Vol
2 CONC . 2: The Western Palatinate. 1985. 405p.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: 97  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT I was born in Erzweiler, Germany and baptized at the Ulmet Parish Church .My wife and I and some of our children were going to America on the ship Samuel when I became ill and died and was buried at sea in the Atlantic Ocean. Some
2 CONC  of our children were already in America. 
2 CONT --------------------
