1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peter Bernhard Rempel
2 CONT #3875    
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:	Born: 15 September, 1792,  Elbing, Elbing, Prussia 
2 CONT Baptism:	Baptized: 4 July, 1813,  Tiegenhagen, Gross Werder, Prussia 
2 CONT Death:	Died: 31 October, 1837,  Lichtfelde, Molotschna, South Russia 1,2 (45 years, 1 month, 17 days)
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT Family #2554	Father:  Rempel, Bernhard (#101361) 1764,  Prussia
2 CONT Mother:  Fast, Elisabeth (#100649) About 1766,  Prussia 
2 CONT Family 1:
2 CONT #2553	Spouse:  Berg, Katharina (#5845) 2 May, 1780,  Petershagenerfeld, Gross Werder, Prussia 
2 CONT Married: 24 October, 1813,  Prussia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1 -- +  Rempel, Elisabeth (#3955) 17 July, 1814,  Elbing, Elbing, Prussia
2 CONT 2 -- +  Rempel, Peter (#5847) 17 July, 1814,  Elbing, Elbing, Prussia 
2 CONT 3 --     Rempel, Johann (#5848) 20 September, 1815,  Elbing, Elbing, Prussia
2 CONT 4 -- +  Rempel, Gerhard (#5849) 14 December, 1816,  Elbing, Elbing, Prussia 
2 CONT 5 --     Rempel, Bernhard (#5850) 15 March, 1819,  Lichtfelde, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT 6 --     Rempel, Bernhard (#5851) 20 September, 1820,  Lichtfelde, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT 7 -- +  Rempel, Katharina (#5852) 3 March, 1823,  Lichtfelde, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT Family 2:
2 CONT #2537	Spouse:  Sawatzky, Margaretha (#3858) 18 July, 1808,  Ohrloff, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT Married: 29 September, 1831,  South Russia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1 -- +  Rempel, Anna (#3876) 18 December, 1833,  Lichtfelde, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT 2 -- +  Rempel, Cornelius (#3878) 12 December, 1836
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Note: According to the original Jungfer marriage register he was the 21 year old only son of the late Peter Rempel of Reinland. This is not in agreement with the 1835 Molotschna colony census which gives his name as Peter Bernhard
2 CONC  and the Tiegenhagen baptismal register which gives his father's name as the late Bernhard Rempel. Either there was a clerical error in the marriage record or two Peter Rempel's have been confused. The 1835 census lists him at Lic
2 CONC htfelde #7, and says he came to Russia in 1817, and moved to Lichtfelde in 1819. The entry for Orloff #25 says he moved away from Orloff in 1819. The Cornelius Janzen submission says he died in Lichtfelde. The original "Profiles" 
2 CONC source (by Delbert Plett) gives a middle initial of "B" for all the children. Other sources, including family sources, use the Russian system of giving the father's first name as the middle name. Records written by Gerhard Willems
2 CONC  (b. 17 Jan 1844) #5886 in the possession of his great grandson Gerhard Willems (b. 24 Aug 1955) #498734 give his marriage date to Katharina Berchen as 15 Oct 1813. The original Jungfer marriage records give 5 Oct 1813.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
