1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Immigrated from S Russia Landed New York 07/17/1874
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT https://www.reidgen.com/getperson.php?personID=I7739&tree=ReidFamilyTree
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT It appears he distributed his property among his children at the time of his third marriage.  He was a wealthy farmer.  Maria must have been an attractive vivacious woman to not only have won Isaac" affection, but also to persuade
2 CONC  him to forsake his well-established family village, "Harms darp" in Jansen NE where his children and grandchildren lived, in order to move to far away Steinbach with his young bride.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Johann Johann Harms and Anna Neudorf. Isaac was born in Blumstein, Molotschna, Ukraine, now called Zaporizka Oblast, Ukraine. His first wife was Anna Sawatzky daughter of Cornelius Thomas Sawatzky and Anna von Riesen.
2 CONT
2 CONT  His second wife was Carolina Plett, and the Third wife was Maria L Fast. No children came from the second and third marriages. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  The 1835 Molotschna Census lists him at Blumstein No. 12 and says he moved to Lindenau in 1846. He was one of the original settlers of the village of Alexanderkron, Molotschna in 1854. He is recognized as being one of the most si
2 CONC gnificant supporters of the KG resettlement program for its landless during the 1860s.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was instrumental in founding Markuslandt in 1864.     Isaac moved to Jansen, Nebraska in 1874, and married Karolina Plett the widow of his first wife's uncle Klaas Friesen.  Son Cornelius remained in Russia until 1913 when he 
2 CONC moved to California.  
2 CONT
2 CONT    It appears he distributed his property among his children at the time of his third marriage. He was a wealthy farmer.  Maria must have been an attractive vivacious woman to not only win Isaac's affection but to persuade him to 
2 CONC forsake his well-established family village, "Harms Darp" in Jansen, NE where his children and grandchildren lived, in order to move too far away from Steinbach with his young bride. *Source,  grandmaonline.org
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of his children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius Harms 
2 CONT Isaac Harms        1837-1866
2 CONT Johann S Harms     1839-1884 Jansen, NE
2 CONT Anna Harms Wiebe        1844-1918 (Mrs Klaas Wiebe) Jansen, NE
2 CONT Margaretha Harms   1846-1847
2 CONT Peter Harms        1849-1924 #41791770* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/177549633/isaac_johann_harms Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 16 2024, 4:20:36 UTC''
