2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Birth note: The 1917 Molotschna census gives the birthyear as 1859.
2 CONT Note: The Memrik Colony Birth Registers give his father's first name as Peter in the birth reocrds for his children David, Heinrich, and Justina.
2 CONT Note: Living in Kotlarevka, Memrik around 1900. A Rundschau letter by brother Abraham (3 April 1901, page 2) says Johann was living at Memrik at that time.
2 CONT Note: Johann, working as a postman, and his family are counted in the 1917 Molotschna Colony census living in Gnadenfeld. His family included his second wife age 39 (1878) who was unable to work, a son age 19 (1898) who was recrui
2 CONC ted as a soldier for 15 months, a son age 17 (1900), a son age 6 (1911), a daughter age 23 (1894), and a daughter age 1 (1916).
