1 NOTE {geni:about_me} My family and I received manumission from Zweibrucken, a town that is southwest of Erzweiler, Germany and not very close to Hessen. The notation in the Zweibrucken protocol says "Christian Doll of Irzweiler leaves 
2 CONC for Carolina".  '''''We immigrated to America on the ship Samuel on August 30, 1737 with my wife Catherine and two little children who were born in Germany, Casper and Catherine.  I took the Oath of Allegiance in Philadelphia upon
2 CONC  arrival in the port on August 30, 1737 with my brother Johan Peter Dull.''' I had land in Moore Township (known then as Lehigh Township). I did not stay in that area and moved my family to Worchester Township in Philadelphia Coun
2 CONC ty (now Montgomery Co.). My estate lists my wife and eight children with only my oldest son  Leonard, specifically named in the estate papers.  My children were named in the patent to my land on November 6, 1776 by Lewis Erb, thei
2 CONC r stepfather, as after my death my wife married him. My will probate filed in Register of Wills, Philadelphia, Philadelphia Co, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT --------------------
