2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Record Source: Berlin Document Center A3342 EWZ50., page A078, Frame #236
2 CONT Record Source: Rempel, Nelly; Gedcom Nelly Rempel - Gedcom: P.O. Box 4, Port Robinson, ON L0S 1K0, nellyr@vaxxine.com 82,522 names. Created 12 Nov 2001.
2 CONT Birth Source: Die Mennonitische Rundschau Note: Most issues are available online at archive.org https://archive.org/details/pub_die-mennonitische-rundschau; Elkhart, IN 1880-1908; Scottsdale, PA 1908-1923; Winnipeg, MB 1923-2007.,
2 CONC  15 Nov 1933, p8 View Page
2 CONT Note: Died After Painful Bladder Disorder And Ezema. Johann studied for two years in the advanced Steinbach Zentralschuchle (High School) in the Molotschna and then began teaching at the age of 18 in the village of Margenau where 
2 CONC he also married. He also taught at an estate in Falz Fein; between 1856-1885 he was called to teach in the progressive village of Ohrloff. Later he worked his farm in Ohrloff to make ends meet. As a teacher Johann introduced new R
2 CONC ussian textbooks into the curriculum as well as a standard German collection of literature with the Lesebuch (reader) edited by the German professor of pedagogy, Karl Kehr. Johann was respected as a prominent teacher in his own ri
2 CONC ght, and "was often consulted in educational matters, like the establishment of the teacher training section of the Halbstadt [Molotschna] Zentralschule [Secondary School]. A number of the best educated men in Ohrloff and elsewher
2 CONC e considered themselves as his best friends" (J. Dyck, Braeul Genealogy, 1983, 22).
2 CONT
