1 OCCU Aeltester (Bishop)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Braun
2 CONT #176629 ♂ /029ja
2 CONT Birth:	Born: 9 August 1791, Chortitza Colony, South Russia
2 CONT Baptism:	Baptized: 1813
2 CONT Death:	Died: 15 December 1868, South Russia (77 years, 4 months, 7 days)
2 CONT  Last update of Individual data: 28 June 2024
2 CONT Parents: Family #104318	
2 CONT Father: Braun, Jacob (#198120) About 1750, Prussia
2 CONT Mother: Reimer, Christina (#198116) About 1772, Prussia
2 CONT Family :  #55786	
2 CONT Spouse: Leike, Susanna (#199328) 20 September 1796, Rosenthal, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT Married: 6 January 1814, Chortitza Colony, South Russia
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT    1 --    Braun, Katharina (#86559) 4 March 1815, South Russia
2 CONT    2 -- + Braun, Jacob (#177429) 13 October 1816, Schoeneberg, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT    3 -- + Braun, Abraham (#201748) 18 January 1819, South Russia
2 CONT    4 -- + Braun, Justina (#186422) 18 September 1821, South Russia
2 CONT    5 -- + Braun, Johann (#219695) 20 October 1823, South Russia
2 CONT    6 -- + Braun, Katharina (#185564) 31 December 1825, South Russia
2 CONT    7 -- + Braun, Susanna (#186845) 14 March 1828, South Russia
2 CONT    8 --    Braun, Heinrich (#186846) 21 October 1830, South Russia
2 CONT    9 -- + Braun, Peter (#185567) 12 November 1832, South Russia
2 CONT    10 --    Braun, Maria (#86575) 11 July 1837, South Russia
2 CONT    11 -- + Braun, Margaretha (#180333) 15 November 1839, South Russia
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Note: In the Oct 1816 Chortitza Colony Census he is listed at Schoeneberg #4. 
2 CONT He was called to the ministry in the Gemeinde in Chortitza, South Russia on October 2, 1824 in Schoeneberg.
2 CONT In the 1835 Chortitza Colony Census he was also listed at Schoeneberg #4. 
2 CONT He apparently moved to Schoenthal, Bergthal Colony with the first settlers of that village about 1837 since he and his family are among a group of Mennonites who expressed a desire to settle in Schoenthal per Odessa Archive, Fond 
2 CONC 6, Inventory 1, File 4889. 
2 CONT He was called as Aeltester in the Gemeinde in Bergthal, Bergthal Colony, South Russia on April 25, 1840 and was the first aeltester of the Bergthal church. 
2 CONT National Archives microfilm #T81 610, p. 5401367 states he died 18 Dec 1868. 
2 CONT He was married 50 years and 8 months. 
2 CONT He had 13 children, 55 grandchildren, and 24 great grandchildren when he died. 
2 CONT As a minister he led 300 funerals, performed 150 weddings, held 60 communion services in which he baptised 797 members, and preached 900 sermons. He was a minister for 15 years and was an Aeltester for 29 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Copied from GRanDMA December 28, 2025
