2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT LISTED AS DAUGHTER OF PETER 
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration:	3 May 1903, S. S. Montrose; arrived Quebec City, Quebec
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST MARRIAGE - Jacob  Thiessen  
2 CONT HISTORY OF JACOB - as taken from Find a Grave Profile for Jacob Toews,with thanks. 
2 CONT "Further waves of Mennonite immigrants continued to arrive from Russiato Manitoba during the 1900s. My mother's parents, the Jacob Thiessens's, arrived in Manitoba in the spring of 1903. Grandfather Thiessen bought a farm 2 miles 
2 CONC north of Winkler. This farm already had a seeded crop growing at the time of purchase. He was very pleased about their move to Canada, however, he did not live long enough to harvest his first crop; he died of cancer." 
2 CONT SECOND MARRIAGE - 1909 - Widower Jacob Toews  - Anna's daughter Maria also married Jacob's son - 
2 CONT Marriage of Anna's daughter - Maria Thiessen marriage to Deidrich D. Toews son of Jacob Toews - November 29, 1903. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Anna - 
2 CONT " Grandfather Toews, who had been widowed in October 1909, got marriedto Grandmother Thiessen. They lived together for some time until Grandmother Thiessen/Toews had a stroke and became helpless. She then wentto live with her daug
2 CONC hter Maria and son-in-law Diedrich Toews." 
2 CONT
2 CONT INTERMENT - BURIAL - Greenfarm Mennonite Brethren Church Cemetery, Morse, Moose Jaw Census Division, Saskatchewan, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT PLOT - 1-26
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of Anna - Jacob Toews history is listed as - "In the meantime, Grandfather Toews' health was deteriorating too so he moved in with his daughter Gertruda and son-in-law John Hooge. Grandfather Toews died Februar
2 CONC y 19, 1919. He and his first wife, Gertruda Hiebert Toews, are both buried in the Winkler Cemetery, southwest of Winkler. Their graves are west of the east entrance close to the north boundary. There are two individual tombstones 
2 CONC in gray." 
2 CONT
