1 NOTE {geni:about_me} #46833804:
2 CONT Mrs. Anna Doerksen, 80, widow of Abraham M. Doerksen, died at her home in Meade, Kansas, May 23, 1943. She had been ill only a short time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Harder was born in [Rosenort, Molotschna Colony] Russia, January 6, 1863, the daughter of Johann Harder and Anna (Wiens) Harder. The Harder family lived for a brief time in Persia and Germany before coming to this country abo
2 CONC ut the year 1875 and settling in McPherson County, Kansas.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Abraham M. Doerksen, August 28, 1881. Mr. Doerksen died November 23, 1928. The Doerksen family first came to Meade and community in 1906.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Doerksen had been a member of the Mennonite Church almost 63 years. She was baptized June 6, 1880. She was the mother of 14 children. Surviving relatives are three sons and six daughters: Martin Doerksen (Felt, Oklahoma); Abe
2 CONC  and Pete Doerksen (of California); Mrs. Mary Neufeld, Misses Linne and Susie Doerksen (Meade); Mrs. Tine Doerksen, Mrs. Anna Thiessen, and Mrs. Margaret Sawatzke (California). Surviving also are two brothers and three sisters: Me
2 CONC ssrs. Henry and Jake Harder (Inman, Kansas), Katherina Doerksen (Meade), Elizabeth Franz (Buhler, Kansas), and Marguerite Warkentine (Dallas, Oregon). There are twenty-seven grandchildren and twenty-four great grandchildren who al
2 CONC so survive. Of the grandchildren, the following are members of the armed forces of our country: Elmer Doerksen (China), Randolph Neufeld (Hawaii), Albert Neufeld (Overseas), Francis Doerksen (U.S. Navy) and Miss Velma Neufeld (Arm
2 CONC y Nurse at Buckley Field).
2 CONT
2 CONT A brief funeral service was held at the Fletcher Funeral Home May 25 by Rev. T. R. Layton, First Baptist Church, MEade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Ruth Sutherland sang "Jesus Savior Pilot Me." The main funeral service was held at the M.E. (EMB) Evangelical Mennonite Church twelve miles south of Meade. Rev. H. R. Harms in charge and assisted by Rev. Orlando Wiebe. The bo
2 CONC dy was sent to Turlock, CA for interment.
2 CONT
2 CONT Newspaper Clipping: Mrs. Doerksen passes
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Anna Doerksen passed away at her home Sunday night May 23 at 10:00 o'clock following a short illness at the age of 80 years, 4 months and 17 days. Short services were held at the Fletcher Funeral Home Tuesday afternoon with R
2 CONC ev. T. R. Layton in charge, followed by funeral services at the M. E. Evangelical Mennonite Church conducted by Rev. H. R. Harms and Rev. Orlando Wiebe. Following services the body was shipped to Turlock, Calif. where she was buri
2 CONC ed by the side of her husband. The Fletcher Funeral home was in charge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Genealogical Registry and Database of Mennonite Ancestry (GRANDMA) # 49748* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55761468/anna-doerksen Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartC
2 CONC opy]: ''Feb 1 2022, 3:52:03 UTC''
