1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johann S Rempel was born in Chortitz, Russia. 1874 he moved his family to Canada. They had 9 kids at the time, Helena had been killed by a Lightning. They had 2 more kids, Bernhard and Annie, born in Canada. They m
2 CONC oved close to Gruenthal at first, Johann and Peter stayed in Ontario for the first Winter, where they found jobs. In year of 1890, Peter, Jakob, Franz, Abram, Cornelius and Bernhard, moved to the Westreserve, to find better farmin
2 CONC g land (3-4 miles east of Gretna(Edenthal) ). Shortly after, Franz moved to Didsbury Alberta, Abram to Altona area, Cornelius to Lowe Farm (he lost his wife in 1893, shortly before the move and she was buried in Edenburg cemetery)
2 CONC , and Bernhard to Swift Current, Saskatchewan. Just before the end of the year, Peter moved from Edenthal to Edenburg.(His son was living on the farm in year 1988) Son Johann and his sisters all stayed and farmed in the Ostreserve
2 CONC . 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Came to Canada on SS Moravian Y
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Note: Came to Canada on SS Moravian July 1875</p>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Johann S Rempel, whose descendants are listed in. this book, was born 15 Apr 1830 in Chortitz, Russia. He was the great grandfather of the author of this genealogy. He brought his family to Canada in 1874. He was buried in the Cho
2 CONC rtitz cemetery near the Chortitzer church located north- west of Steinbach. Their two youngest children, Bernhard and Annie were born in Canada.
2 CONT "
2 CONT The whole clan of 11 children (one young girl was killed by lightning in Russia in 1865) settled near Grunthal with their parents. Apparently two of the boys, Johann and Peter, remained in Ontario for the first winter and found wo
2 CONC rk there. The land in the Grunthal area was not very conducive to farming so some of the boys. (Peter Jacob, Franz, Abram, Cornélius, Bernhard) moved to the West Reserve about 1890. They all settled about 3 or 4 miles east of Gret
2 CONC na (Eden- thal) but very soon after that Franz moved to Didsbury Alberta, Abram moved to the Altona area, Cornelius moved to the Lowe Farm area, and Bernhard moved to the Swift Current, Saskatchewan area. Before Cornelius moved to
2 CONC  the Lowe Farm area his wife died (she is buried in the Edenburg cemetery) in 1893. Peter farmed in the Edenthal area until a few years before the turn of the century and then bought a farm in Edenburg where brother George now liv
2 CONC es. (This is being written. 1988 - HR)
2 CONT Johann and his sisters remained on the East Reserve. All were farmers. Johann farmed only for a short time and then became involved in municipal affatis as secretary-treasurer.
2 CONT Johann S Rempel's wife was Margaretha
2 CONT Sawatzky, born 28 January 1833 and died 22 Jun 1914 in Edenburg at her son Peter's home. She is buried in Edenburg cemetery. Peter's home was located
2 CONT mile west of the cemetery on the south side
2 CONT of the Post Road. Her mother was a Penner.
