2 CONT Excerpt from Didsbury Pioneer
2 CONT
2 CONT Franz Rempel
2 CONT Another pioneer of the Didsbury district passed away when the death of Mr. Franz Rempel occurred on Thursday, August 3rd, 1933 at his residence in Didsbury.
2 CONT Franz Rempel, who was 74 years of age, was born in Russia. He came to Canada 58 years ago at the age of 16 and made his home in Manitoba.
2 CONT He was married to Justina Peters 54 years ago and they resided in Manitoba until 1901, when they moved to Didsbury and homesteaded 18 miles southeast of town. They retired from the farm 15 years ago and resided in town.
2 CONT Fourteen children were born of this union, seven of whom preceded him in death. He is survived by his widow; five daughters, Mrs. Henry Bergen, of Namaka; Mrs. W. K. Unran, of Stettler; Mrs. Peter Loewen of Didsbury; Mrs. Albert M
2 CONC ack of Calgary; Mrs. P. Janzen of Didsbury; and two sons, John and Jake of Didsbury.
2 CONT Excerpt from Didsbury Pioneer, Thursday, August 10, 1933, page 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Alberta Death Reg. #404-865
