1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gertrude Regehr
2 CONT #3879 
2 CONT Birth:	Born: 21 January, 1838,  Muntau, Molotschna, 
2 CONT Death:	Died: 19 December, 1920,  Gnadenthal, Molotschna, South Russia 4 (82 years, 10 months, 29 days)
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT Family #2562	Father:  Regehr, Peter Isaac (#101759) 1 December, 1802,  Prangenau, Gross Werder, Prussia 
2 CONT Mother:  _?_, Margaretha (#101760) 18058
2 CONT Family 1:
2 CONT #2560	Spouse:  Woelk, Franz (#126915)
2 CONT Family 2:
2 CONT #2561	Spouse:  Heinrichs, Franz (#126917) 4 August, 1853,  Schardau, Molotschna, South Russia
2 CONT Married:  South Russia
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT 1 --     Heinrichs, David (#783653) 21 December, 1879,  Gnadenthal, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT Family 3:
2 CONT #2558	Spouse:  Rempel, Cornelius (#3878) 12 December, 1836
2 CONT Married: 19 October, 1861,  South Russia
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT 1 -- +  Rempel, Margaretha (#5912) 16 October, 1866,  Tiegerweide, Gross Werder, Prussia 
2 CONT Family 4:
2 CONT #2559	Spouse:  Janzen, Cornelius (#6281) 1838,  Prangenau, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT Married: Aft 1865,  South Russia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1 -- +  Janzen, Cornelius (#6287) 1866,  Muensterberg, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT 2 -- +  Janzen, Peter (#6289) 1869,  Gnadental, South Russia 
2 CONT 3 -- +  Janzen, Gertrude (#6288) 21 February, 1872,  Gnadenthal, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT 4 -- +  Janzen, Heinrich K. (#6290) 5 May, 1874,  Tiegerweide, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT 5 -- +  Janzen, Isaac (#527733) 2 March, 1876,  Gnadenthal, Molotschna, South Russia 
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Note: One record gives her birth date as 21 Jan 1838 as does National Archives microfilm #T81 610, p. 5401270. The Peter Epp & Anna Classen Descendent Chart (from Anne Ens) gives her birth date as 22 Jan 1836, which appears to be 
2 CONC incorrect. EWZ says she was born 18 Feb 1839. Gertruda sister to Peter according to information written by her son Isaak Janzen was hired by H. Willms at Halbstadt as a full-time baby sitter at ten years of age. She also worked fo
2 CONC r H.Riemers at Ohrloff, David Cornis at Blumenort, Sawatsky's, Klassens and Others. She was married three times.
2 CONT User Note: https://archive.org/details/sim_die-mennonitische-rundschau_1914-05-13_37_19/page/14/mode/1up (Pam Klassen-Dueck, 2/12/2023)
