1 NOTE  It is written that Francis Bryan III was born in 1630, Gloucester Co,
2 CONT VA
2 CONT and died in 1694 in Belfast, Ireland.  It isn't likely that the birth
2 CONT place is correct since his father, William Smith Bryan, was deported
2 CONT to
2 CONT Virginia in 1650 when William Smith Bryan was 77 years old.  Francis
2 CONT III
2 CONT would have been 20 years old when the entire family was deported by
2 CONT Ireland to the shores of Virginia in 1650.  Francis Bryan III
2 CONT (1630-1694)--returned to Ireland in 1667 to reclaim family estates in
2 CONT County Clare.  Meeting opposition, he fled to Denmark where he married
2 CONT Sarah Brunker (cousin to Prince of Orange).  While living in Denmark,
2 CONT a
2 CONT son, Morgan Bryan, was born in 1671 or 1681.  Then following the
2 CONT "Bloodless Revolution" Francis returned to Ireland about 1685 where he
2 CONT settled in Belfast and lived to the date of his death in 1694.  It was
2 CONT in
2 CONT Belfast, 1685, that his second son, William, was born.  William Bryan
2 CONT migrated to American in 1718 and it appears that Morgan may have
2 CONT migrated
2 CONT at the same time or about the same time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records support that they had two sons:  Morgan and William who
2 CONT migrated
2 CONT to America but some researchers indicate that they may have two other
2 CONT sons:  Cornelius and David.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:  Bryans, Hortons, and Allied Families by E. C. Manly and
2 CONT History
2 CONT of the Bryan-Cole Family in America by W. B. Cole.
2 CONT
2 CONT See William Bryan and Morgan Bryan's stories for more about this
2 CONT family.
