1 OCCU Trapper and Trader in Furs, Military
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John was one of the original settlers of Somerset County. Early on he was a trapper and trader of furs. He later served in the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT His exact date of birth is unknown thus far, but had to have been born at least fifteen to twenty years prior to the war, making somewhere between 1750 and 1760.(Estimate)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John seved in the military in 1776. He was a private in Captain Rundio's Flying Camp as part of the Philadelphia Militia in the American Revolution. John worked as a hunter and trapper.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Union Cemetery New Centerville (Somerset County) Somerset County Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary Soldier 1775-1783
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Somehow "Doll" became "Dull" in John's lifetime.  John and Elizabeth had eleven children, all born in Pennsylvania, between 1778 and 1795.  Elizabeth and John are buried in the New Centerville Cemetery, Somerset County Pennsylvani
2 CONC a.  John lived to be 82 years old (Elizabeth lived to 95!)
2 CONT
2 CONT contributed by Karen Parker, fifth great-granddaughter
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT I was born near Trappe, Montgomery Co, Pennsylvania and in 1771 I was living with my mother and stepfather, Lewis Erb.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
