2 CONT
2 CONT St. Paul's Red Hill Luth Ch records states that Peter May was a widow er at the time of his marriage to Juliana Mack. Renninger book states that Anna Margaretha (May) Renninger was born "about 1737 in Germany." Therefore, I've lis
2 CONC ted Anna Margaretha as a daughter of Peter May and unknown first wife, along with Anna Eva Barbara, who was age 14 in 1752.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Abstract: MAY, PETER. Upper Hanover, Co. of Phila. Mason. April 2, 1783. August 1 0, 1784. T.17. Wife: Juliana. Children: Juliana Stout, Margareth Renninger, Sarah Myer, Charina, Barbara Schell. Grandchildren: Children of all
2 CONC  the Daughters living and dead. Exec: Juliana May and Son-in-Law John Stout. Wit: Christopher (his mark) Moll, Is. Mock, Junr.
