1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Dyck
2 CONT #182545
2 CONT Birth:	Born: 28 January 1828, Chortitza Colony, South Russia
2 CONT Baptism:	Baptized: 1849
2 CONT Facts & events:	Immigrated: S. S. Canadian; arrived 19 July 1875, Quebec City, Quebec View Ship List 
2 CONT  Last update of Individual data: 12 September 2023
2 CONT Parents: Family #103373	
2 CONT Father: Dyck, Abraham (#175494) 9 March 1785
2 CONT Mother: Neudorf, Kristina (#174958) 9 January 1793, Tiegenhof, Gross Werder, Prussia
2 CONT Family  1:  #108141	
2 CONT Spouse: Peters, Maria (#182546) 12 March 1827
2 CONT Married: 28 November 1849, South Russia 
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT    1 --    Dueck, Abram (#182547) 2 September 1850
2 CONT    2 -- + Dyck, Elisabeth (#182548) 25 December 1851, Kronsweide, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT Family  2:  #108142	
2 CONT Spouse: Lemke, Elenora (#182549) 22 April 1825, Neuenburg, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT Married: 6 June 1853, South Russia 
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT    1 -- + Dick, Jacob K. (#182550) 18 October 1856
2 CONT    2 --    Dueck, Maria (#186623) 24 October 1859
2 CONT    3 -- + Dyck, David (#182551) 31 May 1863, South Russia
2 CONT    4 -- + Dueck, Peter L. (#182552) 22 January 1868, South Russia
2 CONT Family  3:  #107137	
2 CONT Spouse: Derksen, Margaretha (#181155) 14 October 1835, South Russia
2 CONT Married: 15 June 1889, Rural Municipality of Rhineland, Manitoba
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Note: See his letter to the Mennonitische Rundschau (21 Mar 1900, p5). In that letter he states that he immigrated from Sergeyevka (Fuerstenland) to Manitoba in 1875. He was 73 years old and living in Blumenfeld, Manitoba in 1900.
2 CONC  He states that he left 2 children in Russia: Abraham and Mrs. Heinrich Schapansky.
2 CONT Note: Ship's log shows age as 46. 1880 census shows birth date as 9 Feb 1828 n.s. Age 53 in 1881, RW248. 1901 census shows birth as 28 Jan 1828. B97 and A93* also birth DOB as 28 Jan 1828. R288-3 inccrrectly says birth date is 2 F
2 CONC eb 1824. A93* says baptism is in 1849.
