2 CONT #726377 ♂ /223ja	
2 CONT Birth:	Born: 3 January 1862, Burwalde, Chortitza, South Russia  village details 
2 CONT Baptism:	Baptized: 1881, Michaelsburg, Fuerstenland, South Russia
2 CONT Death:	Died: 1927, Orenburg Colony, Russia
2 CONT Parents: Family #191527	
2 CONT Father: Siemens, Wilhelm (#381109) 8 May 1839, South Russia
2 CONT Mother: Sawatzky, Agatha (#581155) 24 October 1841, Rosenthal, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT Family  1:  #303223	
2 CONT Spouse: Bergman, Aganetha (#726376) 2 May 1861, Nieder-Chortitza, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT Married: 28 November 1888, Nieder-Chortitza, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT    1 -- + Siemens, Agatha (#726374) 14 August 1889, Alexeifeld, South Russia
2 CONT    2 -- + Siemens, Katharina "Tina" (#726337) 12 November 1890, South Russia
2 CONT    3 -- + Siemens, Aganetha (#726336) 13 August 1892, Chutor Sawodsk, South Russia
2 CONT    4 -- + Siemens, Jacob (#726335) 13 February 1894, Rosenthal, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT    5 -- + Siemens, Wilhelm (#726334) 15 April 1896, Rosenthal, Chortitza, South Russia
2 CONT    6 -- + Siemens, Justina (#726333) 8 February 1898, Dolinovka, Orenburg, Russia
2 CONT    7 -- + Siemens, Helena (#726305) 30 March 1901, Nikopol District, Ekaterinoslav, South Russia
2 CONT    8 --    Siemens, Anna (#726304) 6 April 1902, Dolinovka, Orenburg, Russia
2 CONT Family  2:  #303249	
2 CONT Spouse: Mook, Lise (#726375) 3 November 1862
2 CONT Married: 1922, Dolinovka, Orenburg, Russia
2 CONT Notes:	
2 CONT Birth note: 1923 Orenburg Census (Dolinovka) p50 records location as Kanzerovka.
2 CONT Note: Orenburg says he married in Nieder-Chortitza and shows birth place for all children except Anna as Chutor Sawodsk [Sawatzky]. After Jacob's mother remarried "she and [her] new husband arranged for 8-year-old son Jacob to wor
2 CONC k for and be brought up by relatives (or others?). This was hard on him--stayed with him all his life". It has been suggested that he may have been born in Burwalde, Chortitza, Russia, and that he may have lived in a few places in
2 CONC  South Russia prior to moving to Orenburg colony ca 1900. 1923 Orenburg Census (Dolinovka) p50 records a settlement date of 1900. Orenburg records show children born before 1900 as born either Chutor Sawodsk or as Alexifeld (but t
2 CONC hat could be same place).
2 CONT Note: Deyevka, Orenburg Colony. Mennonite Church Registers, Series #1, Vol. 2 p 343 says he left the church in 1908.
2 CONT Note: Elma indicates he was a 'good talker and a freighter for the colony -- travelled a lot selling grain, buying cattle for people, etc....was a very musical person (Schemenauer, Elma, internet message, 21 August 1997). Jacob wa
2 CONC s a "horseman, chauffeur, freighter, livestock dealer, merchant, farmer," etc. (Schemenauer, 1998, p. 32). See Mennonite Historian Sep 1998, p3 for review of "Jacob Siemens Family Since 1685" by Elma Schemenauer. 1923 Dolinovka, O
2 CONC renburg list says he was born in Kanzerovka (Rosenthal).
2 CONT Marriage #1 note: Deyevka, Orenburg Colony. Mennonite Church Registers, Series #1, Vol. 2 p 343 records marriage date as 29 Nov 1888.
2 CONT
