2 CONC - +  Bergen, Abram,  25 Dec 1893, #1020372 3 -- +  Bergen, Isaak,  1896, #1204702 4 -- +  Bergen, Johann,  13 Sep 1897, #524020 5 -- +  Bergen, Helena,  1 Dec 1899, #1204706 6 -- +  Bergen, Gerhard,  , #1204454 7 -- +  Isaak, Mari
2 CONC a,  , #1204725 8 --     Bergen, Margaretha,  1902, #1204718 9 -- +  Bergen, Heinrich,  1904, #1204703 10 -- +  Bergen, Franz,  21 Mar 1906, #738313 11 -- +  Bergen, Jakob,  1907, #1204721 12 --     Bergen, Elias,  1909, #1204704 1
2 CONC 3 -- +  Bergen, Margaretha,  8 Sep 1914, #1018503 14 --     Bergen, David,  1917, #1204724 Notes:	 Note: He moved from Schoenhorst, Chortitza Colony to Ekaterinovka, Omsk region, Siberia in 1906. He was ordained as an Elder in Oms
2 CONC k, Siberia in 1912. He was exiled in 1931 for 5 years and on August 7, 1937 he was again exiled and never returned. Der Stammbaum Peters, page 100: ... In Jekaterinowka, Gebiet Omsk, Peter Bergen, so auch vier verheiratten Soehne,
2 CONC  wurden 1937 von der NKVD erschossen ... Zum Stammbaum Peter Bergen (1872-1937), des Aeltesten der Mennonitengemeinde Alexandrowka, Gebiet Omsk, Siberien. Die Angaben sind vorwiegend nach Franz Thiessen, Espelkamp, angegeben. Pete
2 CONC r and Margaretha had ten boys and three girls. See the book Mennoniten in der Umgebung von Omsk by Peter Rahn where a biographical sketch of him is found on p. 74-77. Peter moved to Omsk, Siberia in 1906 and was ordained to the Mi
2 CONC nistry there and was also ordained as an Aeltester in 1912. He was forcibly taken away by the Russians and exiled to Narim, Siberia. Peter and Margaretha had 10 sons and 3 daughters. Isaak Warkentin from Oak Lake, MB was his broth
2 CONC er-in-law. Birth Source: Schoenhorst, Chortitza Colony. Church Register, page 126 Birth Source: Der Bote [Winnipeg, Manitoba]; Winnipeg, Manitoba, page 6 Sep 2000, p20 Baptism Source: Schoenhorst, Chortitza Colony. Church Register
2 CONC , page 126 Source: Harder, Stanley; Gedcom File, Aug 2001 Source: Thiessen, John; Gedcom File, Jan 2002 Source: Kliewer, Henry; Gedcom File, Jan 2002 Source: Quiring, Mary Ann; Gedcom File, Mar 2002 Source: Gedenke des ganzen Wege
