1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob J. Warkentin
2 CONT
2 CONT MONTEZUMA — Jacob J. Warkentin, 79, died Wednesday at his Montezuma home after a short illness. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born March 7, 1893, in McPherson County, he married Anna Harms March 12, 1916, at Meade.  He was a retired grocery owner and had lived here since 1920.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Warkentin was a member of the Evangelical Mennonite Brethren Church, Meade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include the widow; two sons, Orville and Alvin, both Dodge City; two daughters, Mrs. Walter Hacker, Dodge City, and Mrs. Raymond Ratzlaff, Victorville, Calif.; two brothers, Aaron, Auburn, and Henry, Meade; four sisters,
2 CONC  Mrs. Elizabeth Warkentin, Reedley, Calif., Mrs. Helen Zielke, Mrs. Susie Enns and Mrs. Marie Zielke, all Meade; 16 grandchildren and 17 greatgrandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral will be 2 p.m. Saturday at Church of God in Christ Mennonite, Montezuma the Revs Lloyd Ensz and Daniel Koehn officiating. Burial will be in the church cemetery.  Friends may call until 9 tonight at Hulpieu Swaim Funeral Ho
2 CONC me, Dodge Dodge City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Garden City Telegram, Friday, February 23, 1973, pg. 3* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/41899718/jacob-j-warkentin Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 28 2023, 
