1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ༺✿✿✿༻ LOVING MEMORY ༺✿✿✿༻
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon H. Warkentin
2 CONT ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
2 CONT July 26, 1909 – August 26, 1988
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon H. Warkentin, 79, of Salem died Friday.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in McPherson County, Kansas, He moved to Dallas as a child and moved to Salem in 1952. He was a lumber grader for Willamette Valley Lumber Co., now known as Willamette Industries. He was active in choral groups and oft
2 CONC en visited home-bound persons in the Salem-Dallas area. He was a member of the Liberty Gardens Bible Church, Salem, and The Gideons International.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife, Martha, died in 1977. He married Margaret H. Kroese on January 27, 1979, in Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife; son, Walter of Salem; daughter, Luella Hermanson of Phoenix, Ariz.; brother, Eurt of Dallas; and sisters, Marie Frey and Susan Entz, both of Dallas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Monday in the Evangelical Mennonite
2 CONT Brethren Church, Dallas. Interment
2 CONT will follow in Dallas Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributions may be made to Gi-
2 CONT dons or the Liberty Gardens Bible
2 CONT Church memorial fund.
2 CONT Visiting will be from 1 p.m. to 5 p.m.
2 CONT today in Howell-Edwards-Doerksen, Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/28855526/solomon-h-warkentin Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 28 2023, 8:40:24 UTC''
