0 @N6000000001869722962@ NOTE One family record calls her "Susanna Fehr."  One family record suggests that she may have been born in 1741.  The Helga Enns submission says she was born in "1741" and died 2 Mar 1803. Irene Puttkammer (1996, written comm.) indica
1 CONC tes Susanna was born 1749 and died 2 March 1825, while Schapansky (1992, p. 118) indicates that Susanna was born 6 April 1742 and was from Scharpau.  Adolf Ens (via Margaret Ewert) shows her birth as 2 March 1741.
0 @N6000000001870489304@ NOTE One record says she died 18 Mar 1823.  Her age is incorrectly given as 30 in the Oct 1816 Census.
0 @N6000000001869722906@ NOTE He migrated from Danzig, Prussia to South Russia in 1788 with his father and settled in Rosenthal, Chortitza, S. Russia in 1789 (P. Rempel, p. 41; Danzig Mennonite Church Family Book, Vol. 1, p. 6; Chortitza Colony church records;
1 CONC  B. H. Unruh, p. 266).  In the 1808 Chortitza Colony Census he is listed in Rosenthal among the landless (B. H. Unruh, p. 266).  He was residing in Chortitza, Chortitza Colony in 1814 per the 1814 Chortitza Colony Vaccination List
1 CONC s.  In the Oct 1816 Chortitza Colony Census he is listed in Rosenthal among the landless.  Henry Schapansky says Gerhard died on 30 April 1812 (Mennonite Migrations, p. 555).
0 @N6000000001500501169@ NOTE BIRTH: Richard S. Simpson, Ph.D., "History of the Gmelin Family in Pennsylvania" The Bulletin of the Historical Society of Montgomery County, Vol. XXXIV, No. 1, 2004, pp. 93-109.
