0 @N6000000001870489364@ NOTE One record calls her "Susanna Sawatzky."  The Bergthal Gemeinde Buch (Steinbach: Hanover Steinbach Historical Society, 1993), p. 37, gives a different set of parents for Susanna.  Date of birth is from Schapansky's The Old Colony 
1 CONC (Chortitza) of Russia. The  "Genealogy of the Bergen Family" M. Neufeld, 1979 - Friesen Printers, Altona, gives her death date as 3 Mar 1863.
0 @N6000000001870489485@ NOTE In the 1835 Molotschna Colony Census he is listed at Marienthal #26 and is said to have transferred to the Chortitza Colony in 1836.  He transferred to Einlage, Chortitza Colony in 1836 per Odessa Archive, Fonds 6, Inventory 1, Fi
1 CONC le 4127.
0 @N6000000001869722927@ NOTE One family record calls her "Aganetha." One record says she died 14 Apr 1877.  The Helga Enns submission says she was born 8 Feb 1785. Schapansky finds Agatha born on 8 Sept 1785 (1992, p. 114), although the G. Reimer collection c
1 CONC onfirms 8 February 1785. The Helga Enns submission says she was born 8 Feb 1785.
0 @N6000000001869722769@ NOTE One family record says he was born 2 Feb.
1 CONT Johann and Barbara had no children (Rempel, D., 1969, p. 4).  Margaret Ewert indicates that Johann was born on 18 Mar 1818 (pers comm, 31 Aug 1997). Christine Neufeld (1980, p. 25) reports that Johann, a widower, "brought doom to 
1 CONC the family.  Sawatzky pushed the children from the home and cheated them of their inheritance".
0 @N6000000001370322015@ NOTE The parents family record stated the birth date to be 21 Aug 1628.
