0 @N6000000001869707782@ NOTE He lived in Schoenhorst, Chortitza. Jacob and Anna are listed in the 1897 Vassilyevka, Naumenko Settlement census with their son Gerhard and daughters, Katharina, Margaretha, Eva and Maria. They moved to Naumenko from Chortitza.
0 @N6000000001870488868@ NOTE R318-2  Another source has birthdate as 16 Oct 1844 (West Reserve Bergthal Church Register, No. 1, p.31 and 325). Another source has n.s. marriage date as 24 Oct 1865. One record says he died 19 Feb 1919. SUV-138 says he was born 
1 CONC 22 Sep 1844. Resident of Winkler, Manitoba, Canada. In the 1873 Yazykovo Colony Census he is listed at Adelsheim #33. Another source has n.s. marriage date as 24 Oct 1865. One record says he died 19 Feb 1919.
0 @N6000000001870496203@ NOTE Henry, with his family, was one of the original settlers in Yazykovo, a Chortiz daughter colony established in 1869 on land purchased from the Russian nobility. Henry died of typhus; when he became ill in 1919, his son Jacob came 
1 CONC from Eichenfeld with most of his family to look after the Rempel wirtschaft in Nikolaifeld, thus escaping the Machno massacre. The Vincent Rempel submission says he died 20 Jan 1918.  Rempel also states he was married in Rosenthal
1 CONC , Chortitza. The Schoenhorst register (p. 87) notes that Heinrich moved from Schoenhorst, but the destination is unclear.
0 @N6000000001870496222@ NOTE One family record says he was born in 1837 and died on 11 June 1919. One family record also says he died 6 Dec 1919 in Neuendorf. The Schoenhorst register (p 126) notes that Peter and the family moved to Neuhorst.  Died of typhoid
1 CONC .
