0 @N6000000001869713579@ NOTE (Medical):Had diabetes and eventually had both legs amputated.
0 @N6000000001869708489@ NOTE Remained in Russia.
0 @N6000000001870482211@ NOTE One record gives her birth date as 1 Jan 1873. p. 51 of the Katie Regehr Buller book gives her birth year as 1874 She was widow Regier when she married Johann Pauls.
1 CONT Bethel Inman II p. 68: "November, 1937 Attest nach Brudertal Meade, Kansas." p. 69: baptized by Heinrich Toews.
1 CONT Former Meadean Dies Tuesday at Home in Inman
1 CONT    Mrs. Helena Pauls, 75, former resident of Meade, died at her home in Inman, KS, on Tuesday of a heart ailment.  She had been ill most of the winter.
1 CONT    Funeral services will be held Sunday at 2 p.m. at the Bethel church, south of Inman.  Interment will be in the south Inman cemetery.
1 CONT    Mrs. Pauls was born in southern Russia on Jan. 1, 1974.  She was a member of the EMB church, and lived there until about a year ago.
1 CONT    She is survived by her husband, John J. Pauls; four sons, H. T. Regehr, Portersville, CA; Jake Regehr, George T. Regehr and Curt T. Regehr; four daughters, Mrs. J. H. Buller, Mrs. F. A. Pauls, Mrs. George Becker and Mrs. Jake B
1 CONC ecker, all of Inman; five step children, Isaac N. Pauls, Dallas, OR, Mrs. Jake Sawatsky, Weatherford, OK, Jacob N. Pauls, Minneola, Susie Pauls, Warner, OK, and Pete N. Pauls, Meade; a brother, John Thiessen, a missionary in India
1 CONC , 27 grandchildren and 14 great grandchildren.
